WEBVTT

00:01.543 --> 00:02.377
I've decided.

00:03.002 --> 00:04.587
You're my protagonist.

00:05.672 --> 00:06.840
Ready!

00:12.512 --> 00:16.474
This is... a movie!

00:19.728 --> 00:22.689
Everybody! Please take your clothes off!

00:23.648 --> 00:24.566
All yours.

00:24.649 --> 00:25.567
I'm in!

00:26.484 --> 00:30.155
<i>You see, sewing happens to be my thing!</i>

00:32.574 --> 00:33.908
What quick-thinking!

00:33.992 --> 00:36.077
What an epic recovery!

00:36.786 --> 00:40.790
This is phenomenal!

00:53.595 --> 00:55.430
I can no longer shoot my film.

00:58.850 --> 01:00.226
What reason do I have left...

01:01.061 --> 01:02.395
to live?

02:36.322 --> 02:39.951
EXAM, STAGE THREE

02:40.952 --> 02:43.163
Is this still part of the exam?

02:43.955 --> 02:45.957
Two, four, six...

02:46.583 --> 02:48.668
Man, we lost a lot of people.

02:49.168 --> 02:52.422
Thinking of which,
where'd that stupid film director go?

02:53.214 --> 02:55.133
Thank goodness you're all safe!

02:55.967 --> 02:59.721
Honestly, I think
it's a miracle that I survived.

03:00.388 --> 03:03.433
Now that we've gotten this far,
let's all pass,

03:03.516 --> 03:06.477
and be... classmates!

03:06.561 --> 03:09.772
I mean, I'm gonna pass anyways.

03:10.565 --> 03:11.774
Classmates...

03:12.567 --> 03:15.236
I wonder if they have
school festivals and stuff.

03:15.320 --> 03:16.279
They do.

03:16.905 --> 03:19.282
Sports festivals and school trips, too.

03:19.365 --> 03:20.533
Oh, really?

03:20.617 --> 03:21.743
Hey!

03:22.327 --> 03:23.870
You guys!

03:25.747 --> 03:28.583
Look what I got! I found one on the beach.

03:28.666 --> 03:31.127
This means I pass the second stage, too!

03:31.210 --> 03:32.378
Who's that?

03:32.462 --> 03:33.296
No clue.

03:33.379 --> 03:35.632
We were holding the same parachute!

03:35.715 --> 03:37.634
Kill Baby, remember?

03:39.469 --> 03:42.222
Damn it, we've lost way too many.

03:42.305 --> 03:43.473
Then again,

03:43.556 --> 03:47.477
we only ever take two or three candidates
from the transfer exam, anyway.

03:47.560 --> 03:49.938
For the next stage, let's choose something

03:50.021 --> 03:51.606
that won't kill people as much.

03:51.689 --> 03:52.941
Agreed.

03:53.483 --> 03:54.734
Lead Examiner Usami,

03:56.027 --> 03:59.656
the others should be arriving any minute.

04:02.367 --> 04:03.618
Awesome.

04:04.202 --> 04:05.411
Thank god for that.

04:05.995 --> 04:08.164
'Kay then, let's get started.

04:08.748 --> 04:12.502
Contestants, thank you for your patience.

04:13.086 --> 04:15.880
Before we begin the third stage of exams,

04:15.964 --> 04:18.007
we'd like to introduce
some new participants.

04:18.091 --> 04:18.925
Huh?

04:24.264 --> 04:27.809
OMG, you guys are like super serious.

04:27.892 --> 04:30.186
And the whole gangster look? Big yikes.

04:30.270 --> 04:33.690
Shut up. I don't want to hear
that high-pitched voice.

04:35.275 --> 04:37.568
So, these three will be joining us

04:37.652 --> 04:40.947
from the third stage
as special recommendation candidates.

04:41.030 --> 04:43.741
This is Mr. Kaji, Ms. Toramaru,
and Mr. Shinaya.

04:43.825 --> 04:45.285
SHINAYA - TORAMARU - KAJI

04:45.368 --> 04:46.869
I'm like, so nervous.

04:47.453 --> 04:49.706
Hi guys, I'm Toramaru. Nice to meet you!

04:49.789 --> 04:50.999
Special recommendation?

04:51.582 --> 04:52.542
No way!

04:52.625 --> 04:54.502
You can't do that!

04:54.585 --> 04:57.588
We've risked our lives to get this far!

04:58.172 --> 05:00.049
You think you can just skip all that?!

05:00.133 --> 05:02.969
Get out of here, you spoiled brats!

05:04.178 --> 05:07.140
Take your stupid keychains with you!

05:07.640 --> 05:09.392
Besides, you don't stand a--

05:12.729 --> 05:15.523
Oh my gosh, you're so dramatic!

05:15.606 --> 05:18.234
Like, are you good? Calm down, okay?

05:18.735 --> 05:22.864
Yeah, so I guess I forgot to mention

05:22.947 --> 05:26.993
these guys have been recommended by
professional hit men and agencies.

05:27.618 --> 05:30.580
So, they've got a proven track record.

05:30.663 --> 05:32.457
Play nice, everyone.

05:32.540 --> 05:33.708
You too, Ms. Toramaru.

05:34.208 --> 05:36.252
We don't want to lose any more people.

05:36.335 --> 05:37.837
No hits without notice, please.

05:38.379 --> 05:40.173
But Mr. Usami!

05:40.256 --> 05:42.300
He made fun of my Sakamoto keychain!

05:42.383 --> 05:43.760
He's my favorite!

05:45.178 --> 05:47.346
Sakamoto? As in, the legendary hit man?

05:47.847 --> 05:50.683
Isn't he on a wanted list with a bounty?

05:50.767 --> 05:53.519
I've heard of people
who are fans of hit men.

05:54.395 --> 05:56.898
We should steer clear of her.

05:57.565 --> 05:58.483
<i>Too dangerous.</i>

06:04.447 --> 06:05.615
It won't go through.

06:06.324 --> 06:08.493
They must be in the middle of the exam.

06:08.576 --> 06:12.371
Right. No phones allowed, I guess.

06:12.455 --> 06:16.000
Are you really sure it's safe?

06:16.084 --> 06:19.587
Inviting a student with no experience
seems like a risk.

06:20.129 --> 06:21.172
I have a feeling

06:21.798 --> 06:23.382
it's the young people

06:23.925 --> 06:26.094
who have the power to change society.

06:27.095 --> 06:29.263
Kashima, you were a teenager
when we met, remember?

06:29.806 --> 06:32.016
And Gaku was even younger.

06:32.934 --> 06:34.060
Was I?

06:34.644 --> 06:35.937
I don't remember.

06:36.020 --> 06:37.355
What a shame.

06:38.106 --> 06:42.193
I think that when we grow older,
we have more baggage that weighs us down.

06:43.027 --> 06:45.071
I bet our new friend

06:45.696 --> 06:47.990
can run incredibly fast.

06:49.033 --> 06:50.952
Did ya read something again?

06:51.577 --> 06:52.829
<i>It's from a movie I saw.</i>

06:54.038 --> 06:57.542
For the third stage,
you'll be working in teams.

06:58.042 --> 07:01.295
Please each choose
one of your bullets and open it.

07:02.505 --> 07:04.465
Mine had a headband in it.

07:04.549 --> 07:05.967
Me, too.

07:06.050 --> 07:08.010
Mine's red.

07:09.804 --> 07:10.847
I got yellow.

07:11.347 --> 07:12.181
Mine's blue.

07:12.765 --> 07:13.975
Everyone have one?

07:14.058 --> 07:16.561
We'll now instruct you where to put it on.

07:17.854 --> 07:19.147
What is this?

07:19.230 --> 07:22.108
You will all be participating in

07:22.191 --> 07:25.153
Team Strategy Tail Tag.

07:25.236 --> 07:26.612
Team Strategy Tail Tag?

07:27.113 --> 07:27.947
What's that?

07:28.030 --> 07:29.824
<i>- The objective</i>...
- Here I come!

07:29.907 --> 07:32.702
<i>...is to acquire each other's tails.</i>

07:32.785 --> 07:36.080
<i>We will test your physical abilities,
intelligence, and teamwork,</i>

07:36.164 --> 07:37.915
<i>- among other skills...</i>
- Gotcha!

07:37.999 --> 07:39.959
<i>...through this unparalleled sport!</i>

07:40.668 --> 07:42.545
<i>- So, normal tail tag.
- So, normal tail tag.</i>

07:43.045 --> 07:44.630
There are seven teams and colors.

07:45.131 --> 07:46.632
You have two days

07:47.216 --> 07:49.552
and a ten kilometer radius
within this forest.

07:49.635 --> 07:52.138
If an enemy takes your tail,

07:52.221 --> 07:55.183
you're considered dead
and you fail the exam.

07:55.725 --> 07:58.102
Did the exam get easy all of a sudden?

07:59.312 --> 08:01.063
- Aha, I see.
- What?

08:01.147 --> 08:04.442
This game may seem
like child's play at first,

08:04.525 --> 08:07.236
but in fact, it simulates real scenarios,

08:07.320 --> 08:09.614
and serves as
team survival training for pros.

08:10.239 --> 08:11.991
The tail around the hip implies

08:12.074 --> 08:15.828
that you should protect the lumbar spine,
the source of all movements.

08:15.912 --> 08:20.249
It must be based off of the SERE program
used in U.S. military training.

08:20.333 --> 08:22.627
It's specialized training for hit men.

08:24.045 --> 08:26.088
I see someone's rather perceptive.

08:26.172 --> 08:27.423
You are correct.

08:29.008 --> 08:31.761
<i>The truth is that
too many people died already</i>

08:31.844 --> 08:33.179
<i>so we don't have a choice,</i>

08:33.763 --> 08:36.015
<i>but, I guess it worked out for us.</i>

08:36.098 --> 08:38.809
You guys are so careless with the exams!

08:39.393 --> 08:40.853
Wait a minute...

08:42.355 --> 08:43.314
Mr. Taro...

08:46.359 --> 08:48.778
<i>Mr. Sakamoto and I are on different teams.</i>

08:53.866 --> 08:55.368
RED
KILL BABY - AKIRA - SAKAMOTO

08:55.451 --> 08:56.410
So this is our team...

08:56.494 --> 08:59.205
I guess I'll have to carry the whole team.

08:59.288 --> 09:00.581
I'll do my best, too!

09:01.082 --> 09:03.417
WHITE
SHIN - MAFUYU - KAJI

09:03.501 --> 09:05.086
YELLOW - BLUE - GREEN

09:05.169 --> 09:07.505
Also, you may use any weapons you want.

09:07.588 --> 09:08.422
ORANGE - PURPLE

09:08.506 --> 09:13.094
Try to get as many tails as possible
before time runs out.

09:15.680 --> 09:18.558
Now, we'll begin the third stage of exams.

09:19.100 --> 09:20.518
Ready...

09:21.352 --> 09:22.395
Go!

09:36.492 --> 09:39.036
In woodland warfare,
take advantage of the terrain.

09:39.120 --> 09:41.664
Let's secure a spot on the hill
and set up traps.

09:42.164 --> 09:43.124
Roger that.

09:43.207 --> 09:47.712
Ooh, this is kinda fun!
It's like sports day at school.

09:47.795 --> 09:50.715
"Purple wins! And the crowd goes wild!"

09:50.798 --> 09:52.008
Sure.

09:52.091 --> 09:53.175
<i>She's so cute!</i>

09:57.972 --> 09:58.806
<i>Shin,</i>

09:59.849 --> 10:02.810
<i>let's meet up somewhere upriver.</i>

10:06.856 --> 10:10.401
<i>Mr. Sakamoto, right now, we're enemies.</i>

10:12.486 --> 10:14.405
<i>If the time comes, don't hold back.</i>

10:15.114 --> 10:16.907
<i>I'll come at full force, too.</i>

10:16.991 --> 10:18.242
Right.

10:22.496 --> 10:24.915
Shin, are you sure?

10:24.999 --> 10:27.543
Staying in a larger group
would make us easy prey.

10:29.545 --> 10:30.588
Besides...

10:30.671 --> 10:31.505
Yes!

10:31.589 --> 10:33.507
This will be my first tail!

10:39.805 --> 10:41.515
I won't grow unless I try on my own.

10:41.599 --> 10:42.433
WHITE - SCORE: 1

10:43.476 --> 10:45.895
'Kay, whatever.

10:50.941 --> 10:52.902
Guys, look what I did.

10:52.985 --> 10:53.944
Killer idea, huh?

10:54.528 --> 10:56.864
I call it the Rabbit Tail Tactic!

10:56.947 --> 10:58.783
Let's not cheat, please.

10:58.866 --> 11:00.368
Who you calling a cheat?!

11:00.451 --> 11:02.995
They only specified where to put it, not--

11:03.079 --> 11:05.039
Right, Mr. Taro? Don't you--

11:08.668 --> 11:11.128
What?! What's wrong?

11:13.047 --> 11:14.340
Mr. Sakamoto!

11:14.423 --> 11:17.301
I want to be just like you.

11:17.385 --> 11:18.511
Do you think I can?

11:19.637 --> 11:21.472
I've got your back, sir!

11:21.555 --> 11:23.307
I'll do whatever it takes to keep up!

11:25.017 --> 11:26.477
Are you crying?

11:26.560 --> 11:27.395
No, I'm not.

11:28.062 --> 11:29.855
I've got no use for crybabies!

11:32.733 --> 11:34.360
Shit... Damn it!

11:34.443 --> 11:36.987
Why is she still following us?
Crazy bitch!

11:37.655 --> 11:38.614
Hmm?

11:39.156 --> 11:41.325
Well, how can I help myself?

11:42.284 --> 11:46.330
I like to pursue my love
rather than being pursued.

11:46.414 --> 11:47.581
Damn it!

11:47.665 --> 11:49.250
Also,

11:49.333 --> 11:51.585
there's that bit of otaku in me

11:52.169 --> 11:55.840
that makes me want to collect
all colorways, you know?

12:00.094 --> 12:02.054
You already have one green tail!

12:02.138 --> 12:04.473
Why are you still coming after us?

12:04.557 --> 12:07.476
I know! I'll go get you
another color instead.

12:08.018 --> 12:10.187
You let me go in exchange. How's that?

12:10.271 --> 12:11.480
Huh?

12:12.064 --> 12:13.732
You don't get it at all, do you?

12:22.741 --> 12:26.162
I need one for display
and one for safe-keeping.

12:27.121 --> 12:31.000
It looks so cute!
What color should I get next?

12:38.174 --> 12:39.341
I spy... white!

12:43.220 --> 12:47.141
The other teams must be
collecting tails as we speak.

12:47.725 --> 12:48.851
Tell me...

12:48.934 --> 12:51.937
Why are we out here eating?!

12:52.480 --> 12:56.692
Food is the best remedy
for when you're feeling sad.

12:56.775 --> 12:59.028
We gotta have some self-discipline!

12:59.528 --> 13:00.571
We're mid-exam!

13:01.155 --> 13:02.448
Come and join us.

13:03.741 --> 13:05.075
Are you even listening?

13:09.497 --> 13:11.373
That's disgusting! What is it?

13:11.916 --> 13:12.791
Wormwood tea.

13:13.417 --> 13:14.627
We found some over there.

13:15.961 --> 13:18.631
Also, what's the deal
with that full-blown house?!

13:19.131 --> 13:20.883
Built a bungalow.

13:20.966 --> 13:22.885
We're not here on a camping trip!

13:30.434 --> 13:31.560
A bug!

13:31.644 --> 13:34.522
- It's just a butterfly.
- Get it off! Get it off of me!

13:34.605 --> 13:36.315
- It's beautiful.
- Get it off!

13:36.398 --> 13:37.691
They creep me out!

13:38.275 --> 13:41.570
I hate their weird fluttering
and erratic movements!

13:41.654 --> 13:42.863
Mr. Baby,

13:43.405 --> 13:46.325
there's a good reason
butterflies move like that.

13:46.909 --> 13:48.452
There are "butterfly flightpaths"

13:48.536 --> 13:51.622
that only butterflies can see,
which they follow.

13:52.289 --> 13:54.542
It has something to do
with their pheromones.

13:55.167 --> 13:56.168
Fascinating.

13:56.252 --> 13:58.671
Whatever! Just get it off me, please!

13:58.754 --> 13:59.588
Damn it!

14:12.393 --> 14:13.227
Huh?

14:13.978 --> 14:17.606
They say you shouldn't
touch a butterfly's wings.

14:17.690 --> 14:18.816
Really?

14:18.899 --> 14:20.901
I had no idea. Shit!

14:20.985 --> 14:21.819
But,

14:21.902 --> 14:23.279
- I still...
<i>- Delicate yet swift...</i>

14:23.362 --> 14:24.321
...think they're creepy!

14:24.405 --> 14:26.323
<i>The butterfly itself was unaware.</i>

14:26.907 --> 14:27.908
<i>This girl is...</i>

14:29.201 --> 14:30.035
Akira,

14:31.912 --> 14:34.206
who taught you the basic moves?

14:36.041 --> 14:37.668
The way you handled yourself midair,

14:38.252 --> 14:39.962
and your movement just now...

14:40.671 --> 14:43.215
You're like a different person
from inside the airplane.

14:44.258 --> 14:45.718
How embarrassing.

14:46.260 --> 14:49.930
I'm absolutely useless
when it comes to combat against people.

14:50.556 --> 14:54.560
The moment I look into my opponents eyes,
I feel weak in the knees.

14:55.728 --> 14:57.396
What a dumb thing to say.

14:58.230 --> 15:00.733
We aren't killing each other
in this stage,

15:00.816 --> 15:01.775
so just relax.

15:02.776 --> 15:05.404
That's so kind of you, Mr. Kink Baby.

15:05.487 --> 15:06.739
It's <i>Kill</i> Baby!

15:11.410 --> 15:13.454
You know, you guys better run, too.

15:14.288 --> 15:16.415
I'm being chased by a crazy woman!

15:17.041 --> 15:19.126
I am not going to die for a dumb exam!

15:20.878 --> 15:22.713
Hey, wait a minute!

15:22.796 --> 15:24.131
- Stop.
- Huh?

15:30.095 --> 15:31.430
Ouch...

15:31.513 --> 15:33.015
What is this?

15:33.599 --> 15:35.476
<i>Stainless steel wire...</i>

15:40.606 --> 15:43.525
I can't believe they fell for that.

15:43.609 --> 15:47.571
Trusting others so easily is
a terrible mistake for a hit man to make.

15:48.113 --> 15:49.114
It could be fatal.

15:49.615 --> 15:51.867
We'll collect the tails
off of the dead bodies.

15:53.869 --> 15:54.787
Fire.

16:00.125 --> 16:03.170
We lost the other team because of you!

16:03.253 --> 16:05.297
Huh? Why would you say it's my fault?

16:06.131 --> 16:06.966
Hey.

16:07.049 --> 16:10.552
You said you didn't want to get wet,
so we avoided crossing the river!

16:10.636 --> 16:12.096
'Cuz it woulda been annoying

16:12.179 --> 16:13.806
- if we got wet again!
- Hey.

16:13.889 --> 16:16.308
We're in a survival setting! You can't--

16:19.812 --> 16:21.939
Ooh, that was cool!

16:22.022 --> 16:25.401
Like, how did you dodge that?
It's like you're a psychic!

16:25.484 --> 16:28.028
<i>She's from the
special recommendation group...</i>

16:30.114 --> 16:34.034
You're so lucky.
I wish I was on the white team, too.

16:34.118 --> 16:36.161
White is the color of my Sakamoto!

16:36.245 --> 16:39.415
That's why I really, really, really

16:39.999 --> 16:42.167
have to get white.

16:42.251 --> 16:43.752
Creepy otaku.

16:52.678 --> 16:55.639
Rude. That lowkey hurt my feelings.

17:00.060 --> 17:02.396
This was hand-made!

17:08.485 --> 17:10.446
Mr. Taro, you're bleeding.

17:11.030 --> 17:12.990
That's a really sturdy apron.

17:14.867 --> 17:15.909
<i>It won't budge.</i>

17:16.702 --> 17:18.787
<i>It's driven in pretty firmly.</i>

17:19.538 --> 17:22.875
They don't seem to have
any projectiles, at least.

17:22.958 --> 17:24.835
But they're tougher than we thought.

17:24.918 --> 17:29.339
No need to worry.
It's merely matter of time now.

17:29.423 --> 17:32.342
We don't want a dying rat to bite back.

17:32.426 --> 17:35.262
I'm sorry, guys!
This is all because I'm so senseless.

17:35.846 --> 17:37.347
What are we going to do?

17:39.099 --> 17:39.933
Ow!

17:42.352 --> 17:43.187
Huh?

17:43.854 --> 17:46.356
I guess I... got out?

17:46.440 --> 17:47.608
You're so thin...

17:51.320 --> 17:53.238
Mr. Taro! Mr. Baby!

17:57.159 --> 17:58.160
Run.

18:00.746 --> 18:02.915
Stop, you're going to kill them.

18:02.998 --> 18:05.918
It's fine. We'll do what we have to.

18:06.001 --> 18:07.795
I've seen plenty of hit men fail

18:07.878 --> 18:10.589
because of mercy for their enemies.

18:11.465 --> 18:13.217
Besides, having them dead

18:13.300 --> 18:17.137
would be the safest way to get their tails
without facing resistance.

18:17.888 --> 18:19.848
What should I do?

18:21.934 --> 18:22.893
We'll catch up.

18:23.393 --> 18:24.311
Go ahead.

18:24.937 --> 18:26.313
If I just stretch it a bit...

18:26.396 --> 18:28.816
There's no way you can get through.

18:28.899 --> 18:30.818
I have to fight...

18:33.195 --> 18:34.071
I need to...

18:35.864 --> 18:36.907
I need to...

18:45.374 --> 18:47.793
They say that, among wild animals,

18:47.876 --> 18:50.420
the one who breaks eye contact first,
is the loser.

18:51.421 --> 18:54.550
I wonder how it is for hit men?

18:55.676 --> 18:57.177
<i>I don't think I can...</i>

18:57.261 --> 18:58.178
<i>I...</i>

18:59.346 --> 19:01.557
<i>I don't want to hurt people.</i>

19:04.017 --> 19:06.979
Sometimes, it's okay to run
from things you don't want to do.

19:08.897 --> 19:09.857
Don't worry.

19:10.816 --> 19:11.984
We'll be all right.

19:13.610 --> 19:15.320
<i>Don't worry, Akira.</i>

19:17.072 --> 19:18.490
<i>I'll be alright.</i>

19:19.658 --> 19:24.538
<i>I don't want to just stand by any more
and lose the people I care about...</i>

19:26.248 --> 19:27.207
<i>That's right...</i>

19:28.083 --> 19:29.334
<i>I have to do it.</i>

19:30.002 --> 19:31.795
<i>Otherwise, these people will die.</i>

19:33.547 --> 19:35.007
<i>Pull yourself together, Akira!</i>

19:36.008 --> 19:37.050
<i>Open your eyes.</i>

19:38.802 --> 19:40.554
<i>If the alternative is losing someone,</i>

19:43.015 --> 19:43.974
<i>then I...</i>

19:50.230 --> 19:51.356
<i>I'd rather be an assassin.</i>

20:01.992 --> 20:02.826
What?

20:19.218 --> 20:21.053
Calm down, Akira.

20:22.971 --> 20:23.889
Mr. Taro...

20:25.557 --> 20:26.391
Mr. Taro?

20:26.892 --> 20:27.726
What was I--

20:31.355 --> 20:32.439
Don't talk.

20:35.025 --> 20:38.070
<i>A precise spear-hand attack to
the carotid artery and philtrum.</i>

20:39.404 --> 20:42.199
<i>He's bleeding profusely
and struggling to breathe.</i>

20:42.950 --> 20:44.701
<i>He'll die if not treated soon.</i>

20:46.119 --> 20:48.997
Hey, what'd you do? That was excessive!

20:50.624 --> 20:51.708
No!

20:51.792 --> 20:52.918
This wasn't...

20:53.502 --> 20:55.045
I didn't mean to.

20:56.004 --> 20:56.964
I just...

20:57.047 --> 20:59.299
I just wanted to save you two.

20:59.967 --> 21:01.760
I wasn't...

21:02.678 --> 21:03.929
I didn't...

21:05.013 --> 21:06.390
I'm sorry.

21:07.057 --> 21:08.600
I was so desperate,

21:09.268 --> 21:11.979
I just followed the "path" I could see.

21:14.356 --> 21:16.566
<i>Sakamoto, Nagumo,</i>

21:17.150 --> 21:19.111
<i>you know how if you stare at the target,</i>

21:19.194 --> 21:22.030
<i>you can sometimes see
that "path" to killing them?</i>

21:24.491 --> 21:26.034
<i>Wait? Seriously?</i>

21:26.118 --> 21:28.412
<i>Isn't this a common thing?</i>

21:29.121 --> 21:29.955
Akira,

21:30.622 --> 21:33.125
what's your family name?

21:35.419 --> 21:36.253
It's Akao...

21:37.421 --> 21:39.965
My name is Akira Akao.

21:44.094 --> 21:46.179
I only heard about you three,

21:46.263 --> 21:49.683
<i>Sakamoto, Nagumo, and Akao.</i>

21:53.937 --> 21:55.063
<i>Akao...</i>

23:23.860 --> 23:25.862
Subtitle translation by Yuka Kristi
